  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 3,
  "sortOrder": 59003,
  "verseCount": 18,
  "aliases": [
    "Jas",
    "Jam",
    "Jm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "My brethren, be not many masters, knowing that we shall receive the greater condemnation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For in many things we offend all. If any man offend not in word, the same is a perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Behold, we put bits in the horses’ mouths, that they may obey us; and we turn about their whole body.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Behold also the ships, which though they be so great, and are driven of fierce winds, yet are they turned about with a very small helm, whithersoever the governor listeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Even so the tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things. Behold, how great a matter a little fire kindleth!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And the tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity: so is the tongue among our members, that it defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the course of nature; and it is set on fire of hell.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For every kind of beasts, and of birds, and of serpents, and of things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed of mankind:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But the tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil, full of deadly poison.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Therewith bless we God, even the Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the similitude of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Out of the same mouth proceedeth blessing and cursing. My brethren, these things ought not so to be.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Doth a fountain send forth at the same place sweet water and bitter?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Can the fig tree, my brethren, bear olive berries? either a vine, figs? so can no fountain both yield salt water and fresh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Who is a wise man and endued with knowledge among you? let him shew out of a good conversation his works with meekness of wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But if ye have bitter envying and strife in your hearts, glory not, and lie not against the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "This wisdom descendeth not from above, but is earthly, sensual, devilish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:3:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 3:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:3:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
